\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A top term that a square can lose}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For two pairs of odd generators, the paired exponential
in \ref{fdip-008H} contains the product
#{\psi_1\bar\psi_1\psi_2\bar\psi_2}. In characteristic #{2},
the square of #{\psi_1\bar\psi_1+\psi_2\bar\psi_2} is zero,
although that top product remains a basis word. How can a finite
construction retain the top term without recovering it by
division by #{2}?}
